  "development_selection": "Only the known two-object event apparatus was used for budget selection. The first declared allowance, 64 observations/12000 compute, produced actual fine measurements, structural experiments and a refuted frozen confirmation. It remained unresolved. The two larger candidate allowances were not run. The renamed successor independently learned a relation program under its ordinary 384/360000 allowance. Preserve cold_0 and successor_0.",
  "initial_contract": "Start every stream with empty knowledge. A uses 64 rows/12000 compute/768 meter; B uses 384/360000/4608 and renamed measurement fields on the same physical apparatus. All programs, parameters, source definitions and relation methods are learned from paid observations through ordinary public interfaces; no private formula supplies an agent candidate.",
  "schedule_contract": "Complete all first visits before actual revisits. Keep the original paid observations, object transitions, structural and relation frontier when resuming A. Same stream resource cap is the sum of first-visit allowances, not an extra revisit allowance. All source learning, screening, candidate fitting, failed research and real measurements count.",
  "knowledge_ablation_contract": "After the knowledge arm finishes, replay only its task positions and incremental resource allocations with each old task's own first-visit library and candidate=None. Do not supply successor definitions, candidate programs, proposed probes or prediction scores. Clip allocated resources to that control stream's actual remaining pool. A matched schedule deletion of knowledge is not a separately autonomous scheduler baseline.",
  "persistence": "JSON restore complete state between visits. Initial task histories remain immutable snapshots; results contain each unique task's latest cumulative report, preventing double counting.",
  "evaluation_contract": "After every arm and root has ended learning, score both initial and latest models on the same 4x48 fresh random trajectories and public focus-cut/pair-distance probes. No test uses the true relation radius. Buy one legal fine/coarse/command view sufficient for both models, project paid observations and controls without repurchasing, and separately report each deployed model's channel cost. A task passes only when both random and boundary MSE <=1e-6. Unresolved and already-completed roots all remain in scoring; no outcome changes learning.",
  "scope": "Eight prospectively fixed independently parameterized apparatus roots, with two replicates of each 2/3-object by focus/event combination. Existing public object roles, measurement views and relation operators are supplied by the project. Not a new open-world benchmark.",
  "formal_evidence": false
}
